{
  "chapter": "tools/idempotency",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "Three outcomes, and the third is the common one. Most network timeouts happen on the",
    "response rather than the request, so 'unknown' is not a coin flip: it skews toward it",
    "happened, which is the direction that costs money.",
    "There is no protocol fix. The only move is to make the question stop mattering, by",
    "designing the operation so that doing it twice and doing it once produce the same world.",
    "Two different things repeat a call. Your infrastructure knows it is repeating; the model",
    "does not, because a repeat is a fresh judgement made without memory of a call in flight.",
    "So the key cannot come from the model. It is derived from the run, the tool name and the",
    "canonical arguments \u2014 every term available to your code.",
    "Deduplication is silent for infrastructure and must never be silent for the model: a",
    "repeat comes back saying it was already applied, so the model stops asking.",
    "Arguments here are flat strings and integers, and the key is the first 16 hex characters",
    "of a SHA-256, so both tracks derive byte-identical keys."
  ],
  "config": {
    "reservedArgs": [
      "idempotencyKey",
      "requestId"
    ],
    "keyLength": 16
  },
  "cases": [
